 "observations": [
  "The page number «128» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 17», in bold sans serif, underlined. The titles (L01, L02), in bold, the sigla in roman: L01 that of O, L02 that of C and N; «Ozari», the Arabic name of Mercury. The folios of the manuscripts, «C 51v—52r, O 108v,» over «N 32v..», stand at the left of the titles, the letters raised; here as left margin notes beside L01-L03, divided so that they keep within the page. The page has no signature.",
  "The table: a thick and a thin rule above the head, a double rule below it; vertical rules divide the fifteen columns, double ones before and after the columns of the years and of the months; thin rules under the heads that span the four columns of signs, degrees, minutes and seconds, whose heads «Sig.», «Gr.», «Min.», «Sec.» are set in small bold type, only the first «Min.» and «Sec.» with note numbers. «Anni collecti» and «Anni plani» are printed turned through a quarter, reading upwards, in two lines, «Menses arabici3)» in two lines; here their words stand in L03 and L04. Each printed row is one line here, the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The collected years end with 570 (L25), the months with Dulheia (L17).",
  "L06-L35. The anomaly of Mercury moves by the excess of the conjunctions of Mercury over the sun's revolutions, with Brahmagupta's parameters (17 936 998 984 and 4 320 000 000 in 1 577 916 450 000 days) 3° 6′ 24″ 8‴ a day (p. 56, JP2 0088), 8s 27° 22′ 19.8″ in 30 Arab years (10 631 days). Checked: the 30 single years, 354 days and 355 in the leap years 2, 5, 7, 10, 13, 16, 18, 21, 24, 26 and 29, agree to within 0.5″ (with the readings of notes d-f), the year 30 being 8s 27° 22′ 20″; the months, 30, 59, … 354 days, agree to within 0.2″ (with the reading of note g), the year of the months, 0s 19° 46′ 24″, being the single year 1. The collected years step from the radix 2s 8° 53′ 10″ (68° 53′ 10″) by 8s 27° 22′ 20″, the rounded value, to 480, and run ahead of the computation by up to 3.6″ (with the readings of notes a-c); 510 and 540 step by 19″ and 20″.",
  "L25, the row 570, 3s 18° 57′ 20″: the seconds are 9 less than the step of the table gives from the row 540, 3s 18° 57′ 29″, and 5.7″ less than the computation from the radix, 3s 18° 57′ 25.7″. No note bears on them.",
  "L05, «See.»; the margin note beside L03, «N 32v..»; N04, «Jumedi elawel]» and «Jumedi II]»: see the critical notes. L12: «Regeb.», with a point, as printed. A small tick after the «Sig.» of the months (L05), a speck; not transcribed. N01: «(sic)», the editor's, in italics. The apostrophes of O's abbreviations, «Rab’», «Gum’», «Scab’», «Rath’», «Scaw’», «Dulk’», «Dulh’», as printed. The ellipses «. . . .» of the lemmata as printed. Italics: «sic», «V. notas in tab. 8.»."
 ],
